<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hammir Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1326–<a href="/years/1364">1364</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hammir Singh was a ruler of Mewar who recovered Chittor from the governors of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> around 1326 and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisodia">Sisodia</a> branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guhila-dynasty">Guhila dynasty</a>, taking the title of rana. Head of the Sisodia family, a cadet line named after the village of Sisoda, he rebuilt the power of Mewar, and all later maharanas of Mewar descended from him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hammir-singh.jpg" alt="Hammir Singh" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wmpearl · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rana_Hamir_leaving_Ranthamore_Fort_for_Battle,_Kangra_school_watercolor,_Tokyo_National_Museum.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
